==Norwegian Nynorsk==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|nn|ine-pro|*h₂el-|id=grow}}
From {{inh|nn|non|elda||to make old}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|nn|elde}} (e and split infinitives)

====Verb====
{{head|nn|verb|passive|eldast|present tense|elder|past tense|elde|supine|eldt|imperative|eld|past participle|eld|present participle|eldande}}

# {{lb|nn|transitive}} to make [[old]], have [[look]] old

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|nn|alder}}
* {{l|nn|gamal}}, {{l|nn|gammal}}, {{l|nn|eldre}}, {{l|nn|eldst}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|nn|non|elda||to kindle, fire up}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|nn|elde}} (e and split infinitives)

====Verb====
{{nn-verb-1}}

# {{lb|nn|transitive}} to [[kindle]] (a fire)
#: ''kunne du '''elde''' opp i omnen?''
# {{lb|nn|transitive}} to [[heat]] up
# {{lb|nn|transitive|figurative|by extension}} to [[egg on]], [[provoke]], [[encourage]], [[motivate]]
#: ''han '''elda''' opp krigarane''
# {{lb|nn|transitive|metallurgy}} to [[keep]] (i.e. a metal) inside a fire
# {{lb|nn|intransitive}} to [[emit]] [[spark]]s, [[glow]]
# {{lb|nn|intransitive}} to experience a [[burning]], [[stinging]] [[pain]]
#: ''eg '''eldar''' i halsen''
#: ''det '''eldar''' for brystet''

